  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that RNA-only scvi_n200 with multiprofile and transformer aggregation performs best (0.6530 accuracy, 0.6283 F1), with avgpool nearly as strong. Image-only resnet50 is weak, so it is unclear whether adding image features to the best RNA setting provides any benefit. config_032 tests this directly by adding resnet50 image features via simple concat fusion while keeping the same scvi_n200 multiprofile transformer setup as the best RNA-only baseline. This isolates the effect of multimodal fusion before spending budget on more complex choices such as ViT, weighted fusion, or other RNA encoders."
}

